# Ship policy

Do not ask to push or merge. That confirmation is redundant.

- Commit and push as you go. Open or update the PR. Merge when CI is green and repo rules allow it (`gh pr merge` / GitHub auto-merge). Do not wait for a human "go merge."
- If you cannot merge or push, flag the blocker in one short message: required reviews, failing checks, branch protection, permissions, or conflicts. Fix what you can. Do not ask which option to pick.
- Canonical source of truth is the latest remote push. Fetch first. If local and remote diverge, you decide what to keep: prefer the latest pushed work unless it would drop the task you were asked to finish. Rebase or merge yourself. Never ask the user to choose versions.
